<title>GERMANY: Holzmann appoints new supervisory chief.</title>
<headline>Holzmann appoints new supervisory chief.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's largest construction group, Philipp Holzmann AG, said on Thursday it had appointed Carl von Boehm-Bezing as the new head of its supervisory board.</p>
<p>Boehm-Bezing, also a member of Deutsche Bank AG's management board, takes over from Hermann Becker, who resigned early in March.</p>
<p>The appointment was made at an extraordinary meeting. Harald Rieger, board member of Metallgesellschaft AG, will join the supervisory board.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
